<title>USA: CS First Boston named in lawsuit.</title>
<headline>CS First Boston named in lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS First Boston and an employee at the firm were named in a lawsuit that alleges manipulation of the price of Data Dimensions Inc and Viasoft shares, lawyers for the plaintiffs said.</p>
<p>CS First Boston was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>The lawsuit was filed on behalf of holders of Data Dimensions and Viasoft on June 19-20, the law firms Kaplan Kilsheimer &amp; Fox LLP and Bernstein Litowitz Berger &amp; Grossman said in a statement.</p>
<p>The lawsuit claims the firm had large short positions in each company and then issued a misleading report about the companies, causing the stock price to drop.</p>
<p>CS First Boston is a unit of Credit Suisse.</p>
